profile: runtime-mirust.architecture.v116
updated_utc: 2026-08-02T15:33:24Z
active_product:
  name: TinyRustLM
  root: tinyrustlm/
  goal: 100% custom Rust/WASM browser-local SLM runtime and UI.
  live_public_site: TinyRustLM.com
  public_site_boundary: Runtime.MiRust.com remains project/docs identity; TinyRustLM.com is the live local `.slm` import surface and must not auto-fetch hosted `/models/` bytes; SLMComposer.com is retired historical naming.
current_vector_oracle_foundation_boundary_2026_07_21: `rust/experiments/tinyrustlm-vector-oracle/` is a dependency-free, publish-disabled, unsafe-forbidden scalar experiment crate with no runtime, SDK, packer, browser, model-weight, `.slm`, training, or release integration. Its source-bound receipt `scalar-oracle-foundation-51ab608f417c0b82`, attempt SHA256 `8772ee70a2de21b294fc3d10c2634059c72062e33397472762462d04e7b7938b`, and durable report `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-vector-oracle-foundation-memory-2026-07-21.md`, SHA256 `c85182a9dc88dbf8d04ac249aae3b0301d0c1fd0cabbdce9f961091602a6614c`, prove only checked deterministic generation, signed permutation, power-of-two normalized Walsh-Hadamard, scalar Lloyd codebooks, 1-to-16-bit canonical packing, packed scalar scoring, error metrics, byte accounting, native tests, WASM compilation, and isolation. Static model weights remain unchanged. Do not infer TurboVec parity, TurboQuant implementation, a named quantization arm, native/WASM SIMD performance, retrieval recall, KV-cache fidelity, product adoption, training authority, or release readiness. Third-party review artifacts belong outside the repository and Git. Add named methods only after exact primary-source and license pinning, clean-room vectors, preregistered equal-effective-byte comparisons, and domain-specific sealed gates.
openelm_1_1b_instruct_source_boundary_2026_07_16: Exact apple/OpenELM-1_1B-Instruct revision effd796da2a77361d7360e45e54c7cc14bc5df2a is terminally rejected before weight acquisition under receipt bfe9bf44898b9fa9cb8806cb589d4ddb599be87ff5d321fe3263cc357bab74fb. Its config delegates AutoConfig and AutoModelForCausalLM to publisher Python, both pinned Transformers 5.13.1 native registries lack OpenELM, Apple's official path requires trust_remote_code=True, and the immutable repository publishes no tokenizer or chat template while defaulting to an external Llama-2 tokenizer. A bounded header proves 1,079,891,456 BF16 values in 226 tensors, but the 2,159,808,696-byte weight was not acquired. Do not execute publisher code, acquire the external tokenizer, invent serialization, or add OpenELM loader, tokenizer, template, conversion, runtime, quantization, native-kernel, browser-kernel, P2P, catalog, or legacy compatibility paths.
smollm_1_7b_instruct_source_boundary_2026_07_16: Exact HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM-1.7B-Instruct revision 69f49d9c36434d6a3f319dadc5bd3b812752b98b is rejected at 1/8 before conversion under receipt 3cdcf89746463646083802257760627524c45c80d3fd1fe8ec89d2bf7ee440e8. Its dense Llama shape has 24 layers, 2048 hidden width, 8192 FFN width, 32 query and 32 KV heads, tied 49152-token embeddings, and a 2048-token context; BF16 KV growth is 196608 bytes/token and 384 MiB at full context. The repository has Apache-2.0 metadata but no standalone LICENSE. Do not add conversion, runtime, quantization, native-kernel, browser-kernel, P2P, catalog, or compatibility work for rejected bytes.
granite_4_0_h_1b_source_boundary_2026_07_16: Exact ibm-granite/granite-4.0-h-1b revision d18cca4c121edb87d022116d281ce212c9136f57 is rejected at 2/8 before conversion under receipt 329b346f84ab74ce0141266e3e6cc4d90d3dc1f027c673609062d927c872a907. Its dense shared-MLP hybrid has 36 Mamba2 plus four attention layers, tied 100352-token embeddings, fixed BF16 recurrent/conv state of 27.914 MiB at batch one, and 8192 bytes/token of BF16 attention KV growth. The configured 131072-token ceiling is not browser practicality evidence. The repository has Apache-2.0 metadata but no standalone LICENSE/NOTICE; its supporting Sigstore bundle was only partially validated and is not release authorization. Do not add Granite-hybrid recurrence, cache, scaling, conversion, quantization, native-kernel, browser-kernel, P2P, or catalog compatibility for rejected bytes.
amd_olmo_1b_sft_source_boundary_2026_07_16: Exact amd/AMD-OLMo-1B-SFT revision 228e18a8172beabcce6a0e686ac084cede5820fc is rejected before source-weight acquisition under receipt 59ed6823274b16068057cdc21da110777cb92a0aac54e58978106f8cd73639f4. Native Transformers 5.13.1 can instantiate its 1,176,764,416-parameter tied, 16-layer full-MHA OLMo shape without remote code, but the immutable tokenizer has no chat template, the repository has no chat_template.jinja, and the card defines no system or multi-turn serialization. The card's BOS-from-EOS example conflicts with tokenizer EOS token `|||IP_ADDRESS|||`. Do not invent serialization or add OLMo conversion, runtime, browser, P2P, or catalog compatibility for rejected bytes; no model weight was acquired and no quality run occurred.
minicpm4_0_5b_source_boundary_2026_07_16: Exact openbmb/MiniCPM4-0.5B revision 5253c7fcc5e29e1cf3eacb59a58adf1ba4df8630 is rejected before source acquisition under receipt a913153dcd115cb4b7811c1bdca662eff78721099edefa521a7e50c6f858f81a. Its config delegates AutoConfig and AutoModelForCausalLM to repository Python, the publisher example requires trust_remote_code=True, and Transformers 5.13.1 has no native MiniCPM registry mapping. Public text inspection identified custom LongRoPE, embedding/logit scaling, and depth-scaled residual semantics; a bounded safetensors JSON-header range established the dense tied-embedding tensor shape without acquiring the tensor payload. Do not execute publisher code or add MiniCPM, LongRoPE, residual-scaling, conversion, runtime, or browser compatibility paths for rejected bytes.
gemma_3_270m_it_source_preflight_boundary_2026_07_16: Exact google/gemma-3-270m-it revision ac82b4e820549b854eebf28ce6dedaf9fdfa17b3 is rejected before gated acquisition. No terms were accepted, no credential was requested, and no source model or tokenizer payload was acquired. Current Gemma redistribution controls and prohibited-use policy conflict with TinyRustLM's fixed direct-P2P and lawful-adult product contract. Do not add Gemma runtime, policy, license, P2P, conversion, or browser compatibility paths for this rejected source.
h2o_danube3_500m_source_boundary_2026_07_16: Exact h2oai/h2o-danube3-500m-chat revision c202f976c26875541e738ea978c8158fa536da9a is rejected at 1/8 before conversion. Its Llama-shaped 16-layer dense GQA contract has hidden width 1536, 16 query heads, eight KV heads, head width 96, untied 32000-token embeddings, an 8192-token context, and 49152-byte/token BF16 KV growth. Capture schema v3 binds publisher-template omission of an unsupported system role, the empty effective system prompt, both tokenizer JSON and SentencePiece model, local-only/no-remote-code eager execution, source regex mode, seeds, budgets, and untouched one-call outputs. The source followed a quoted credential-revelation instruction. Do not add a compatibility path for rejected bytes.
h2o_danube2_source_boundary_2026_07_16: Exact h2oai/h2o-danube2-1.8b-chat revision 6d8114cb4160755a092babed10a7d383cc10b1db is rejected at 1/8 before conversion. Its Mistral-shaped 24-layer dense GQA contract has 32 query heads, eight KV heads, untied 32000-token embeddings, an 8192-token context, and 61440-byte/token BF16 KV growth. Capture schema v3 binds the publisher-template omission of an unsupported system role, the empty effective system prompt, both tokenizer JSON and SentencePiece model, local-only/no-remote-code eager execution, and untouched one-call outputs. Do not add a compatibility path for rejected bytes.
zamba2_source_boundary_2026_07_16: Exact Zyphra/Zamba2-1.2B-Instruct-v2 revision 960222dd212c071e2b7e3734573ee5297b1c075d is rejected at 1/8 before conversion. Its hybrid contract has 38 Mamba2 layers and six logical invocations of one shared Transformer block, with position-specific rank-128 adapters, six distinct KV caches, tied 32000-token embeddings, and a 4096-token context. At batch size one, BF16 decode state is a fixed 39.262 MiB plus 98304 bytes/token of attention cache. Capture schema v3 and recorder v8 bind the included system prompt, embedded ChatML template, local-only/no-remote-code eager execution, seeds, budgets, untouched one-call outputs, and tool identities. Do not add a Zamba2, Mamba2, shared-Transformer, adapter, hybrid-cache, conversion, or browser-kernel compatibility path for rejected bytes.
granite_3_1_1b_a400m_source_boundary_2026_07_16: Exact ibm-granite/granite-3.1-1b-a400m-instruct revision 0da7a48b0276d500ce5922fd2b33944091fc6c09 is rejected at 0/8 before conversion. Its GraniteMoE contract has 24 layers, 32 experts per layer with top-eight routing, hidden width 1024, 16 query heads, eight KV heads, tied 49155-token embeddings, and a 131072-token configured context. All 1,334,628,352 BF16 parameters remain resident even though sparse routing reduces active expert compute; BF16 KV growth is 49152 bytes/token at batch size one. Capture schema v3 and recorder v8 bind the included system prompt, publisher template, local-only/no-remote-code eager execution, seeds, budgets, untouched one-call outputs, and tool identities. Do not add GraniteMoE, sparse-routing, Granite-scaling, conversion, quantization, or browser-kernel compatibility paths for rejected bytes.
bitnet_source_boundary_2026_07_16: Exact microsoft/bitnet-b1.58-2B-4T revision 04c3b9ad9361b824064a1f25ea60a8be9599b127 is rejected at 4/8 before conversion. It is a native ternary W1.58A8 architecture with 2,412,820,480 logical parameters, 30 layers, 20 query heads, five KV heads, tied 128256-token embeddings, and 76800-byte/token BF16 KV growth. The 1.0977 GiB packed source exceeds the current browser selector budget, and the runtime has no ternary `.slm` type or BitLinear kernels. Current f32, q8_0, and q4_0 formats are not one-bit models. Do not add a compatibility path for rejected bytes; any future native low-bit lane must be a clean architecture admitted by its own passing source, format, kernel, capacity, fidelity, and quality evidence.
falcon_e_1b_source_boundary_2026_07_16: Exact tiiuae/Falcon-E-1B-Instruct revision d20167318084c330b205e221eceed19354197bdc is rejected at 0/8 before conversion under receipt fa5adab7de514b503f9f33b9f5ee954f0f16d1aa501130570297289f29738c75. Its Llama-shaped checkpoint stores packed ternary 1.58-bit weights with 8-bit activations and BF16 embedding/output tensors; it is not literal one-bit. Native Transformers loading required no publisher code, but compact storage did not override complete behavioral failure. Capture tool v5 preserves publisher stop IDs [11,228] under greedy decoding after retaining the invalid single-EOS capture as process-failure evidence. Custom Falcon terms remain legal-review-required. Do not add BitNet conversion, kernels, browser, P2P, catalog, or legal compatibility work for rejected bytes.
final_attestation_dependency_boundary_2026_07_16: The final predicate must bind every release-gate receipt identity, include the current public secret-scan receipt as a causal dependency without placing derived receipts in the recursive subject set, and use the newest release-gate completion as its evidence cutoff. The immutable final receipt must parent the secret scan and may not predate any parent. Never reduce a release gate to an unbound Boolean.
release_source_history_boundary_2026_08_02: Historical WIP commit 15bcf5049eb8616f856daf8cbc8604b877a7af0b tracked third-party model bytes. The human has now authorized clean-slate history replacement. Integration cleanup commits e452266 and b59f0ba remove generated, downloaded, model-review, package, browser-profile, sysroot, and binary output trees after external hash-bound preservation; current integration commit b59f0ba411aa0d4f6320e1ddda9b49e068d42c4d has only six permitted tiny `.slm` fixtures. Its ancestry remains contaminated, so it is not publishable. Construct a parentless root from the reviewed final tree, then prove reachable-object, path, blob-size, model-byte, secret, build, test, package-input, and public-claim audits before pushing. Preserve old receipts and local refs as historical evidence; do not add compatibility or migration support.
stablelm_source_boundary_2026_07_16: Exact stabilityai/stablelm-2-zephyr-1_6b revision 2f275b1127d59fc31e4f7c7426d528768ada9ea4 is rejected at 2/8 before conversion. Its 24-layer dense shape uses ordinary LayerNorm biases, 25% partial RoPE, full 32-head MHA, QKV biases, untied 100352x2048 embeddings, and 192 KiB/token FP16 KV growth. The current runtime has no exact StableLM profile, and the non-commercial research license excludes production use absent separate authorization. Do not add a compatibility path for rejected bytes.
current_browser_performance_architecture:
  runtime_release_profile: Optimize only `tinyrustlm-runtime` at level 3 while retaining the workspace size-oriented portable release profile.
  q4_kernel: Accumulate each q4 block before applying its scale; preserve deterministic row parity tests.
  prompt_projection: Skip final normalization and vocabulary projection for non-final prefill tokens because only the final prompt logits seed generation.
  prefix_cache: Reuse KV state only when the complete retained token sequence and cache length match and that sequence is an exact prefix of the new prompt with a nonempty suffix.
  fail_closed: Partial-prefix, mismatch, reset, failure, model load, unload, or adapter apply clears reuse authority and requires a full prefill.
  diagnostics: Report reused and computed prefill token counts so browser proof can establish their sum equals the full prompt.
  portability: Do not require SIMD for the default checked WASM; capability-specific binaries need a separate fallback and admission path.
  quality_boundary: Runtime acceleration cannot alter strict output bytes, semantic rubrics, model admission, or model-quality claims.
  deployment_boundary: Checked WASM and manifest are production-deployed with FTPS/HTTPS hash equality; exact-prefix reuse remains unproven for normalized production local-file history and cannot support a broad performance claim yet.
current_q4_simd_architecture:
  scalar_oracle: Keep the checked scalar q4 block kernel and differential tests as the correctness authority.
  native_dispatch: Use AVX2 only after runtime feature detection and only for the validated 32-value block contract.
  wasm_dispatch: Build SIMD128 behind `wasm-simd` into a separate binary; never make SIMD a requirement of the scalar artifact.
  browser_admission: Verify route, byte count, checksum, and `WebAssembly.validate` for the SIMD pair before selection; independently verify scalar fallback.
  storage_boundary: Operate directly on packed nibbles and per-block scales; never retain a model-sized decoded f32 shadow.
  measured_result: Controlled Qwen2.5-1.5B 83-token native prefill improved from about 135 seconds to 16,807 ms with identical argmax/top-32 and logit cosine 0.9999999999569831.
  claim_boundary: Native evidence does not authorize a browser throughput claim, model promotion, or public coherent-conversation claim.
  next_load_contract: Transfer one allocation into runtime ownership, use immutable offset-backed tensor views, copy only tensors made mutable by adapters, stream fetch chunks into WASM, and release deterministically on every failure/replacement/free path.
current_production_conversation_architecture:
  shell_status: Production root, required JavaScript modules, optimized WASM, manifest, and default MiniModel smoke execution are healthy.
  default_boundary: The current 8.6 KiB MiniModel artifact is an execution fixture and must never carry an assistant-quality claim.
  rejected_browser_models: SmolLM2 360M q4 and SmolLM2 135M q8 fail real production multi-turn coherence and cannot become the default.
  next_source_contract: Exact tiiuae/Falcon-H1-1.5B-Instruct revision 80ebc50d7799a440b96c93bb6686a3924a09b0cb is rejected at 2/8 under the current untouched source gate. Its parallel attention-Mamba hybrid, recurrent/conv cache, model multipliers, untied output head, and token-ID asymmetry are unsupported, but no implementation path is authorized for a behaviorally rejected custom-license source. Select a genuinely distinct immutable source and require source, license, tokenizer, template, generation-profile, tensor, and semantic evidence before conversion; pre-release experiments create no compatibility obligation.
  conversion_order: source f32 parity, quantization sensitivity, native behavior, checked WASM behavior, bounded browser loading, MiniModel admission, then default selection.
  quality_boundary: Preserve untouched raw/visible output and known strict failures; runtime success, transformed 12/12 sidecars, nonempty output, or a single preference term cannot promote a model.
  training_boundary: Role-history training remains closed until all 42 records have explicit human decisions and a merge-ready contamination-safe freeze.
current_model_quality_architecture:
  manifest: docs/report-intake/2026-07-11/MANIFEST.md
  synthesis: docs/report-intake/2026-07-11/tinyrustlm-response-quality-footprint-synthesis-2026-07-11.md
  tdd_plan: docs/report-intake/2026-07-11/tinyrustlm-response-quality-footprint-tdd-plan-2026-07-11.md
  durable_memory: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-response-quality-footprint-memory-2026-07-11.md
  current_truth: No model is promoted as the default; exact prompt-token parity is proven, while q4/q8 logits and raw semantic output still fail.
  first_slice: Reference-locked f32 source/native/WASM parity, quantization localization, measured mixed q8/q4 packing, and model-bound sampler fidelity.
  promotion_boundary: Untouched one-call decoder output plus semantic, footprint, browser, network, and visual-lock gates; transformed sidecars cannot promote a model.
  deferred: SLM2, q5/q6, quantized KV, OPFS paging, WebGPU, and custom distillation/QAT follow only after mathematical and raw-quality fidelity.
