e_next_token ErrorCode step-token smoke, free_model smoke, validate_adapter_delta/apply_adapter_delta ABI smoke, focused browser Step Token smoke, focused browser Adapter Sidecar smoke, focused selector-budget, sidecar-budget-contract, module-plan-fetch-policy-drift, module-plan-origin-policy-drift, module-plan-runtime-scratch-drift, module-plan-kv-cache-drift, module-plan-total-budget-drift, module-plan-total-limit-drift, module-plan-resource-drift, module-plan-graph-drift, module-plan-stack-drift, module-plan-role-drift, module-plan-slot-drift, module-plan-phase-drift, module-plan-dependency-drift, module-plan-byte-drift, and module-plan-checksum-drift smokes, desktop/mobile UI audit, three-cycle q8/q4 endurance smoke, multi-token q8/q4 browser performance smoke, three-cycle q8/q4 performance soak, and Visual Studio verified-server reuse plus busy-port fallback are implemented and verified; real trained weights, trained-model quality, trained LoRA modules, and broader offline operators beyond blend, delta, sparse-delta, crossover, mutation, prune, DARE, federated, sign-merge, and soup remain pending.
current_boundary_fetch_count_delta: Generated module-plan routing now also binds `module_plan_fetch_count_limit=32`, renders Module Plan `Fetch Limit`, computes planned self-assembly route count before generated model fetch, and proves `module-plan-fetch-count-drift` before `.slm` or adapter routes.
current_boundary_converted_trained_all_delta: `browser-converted-trained-bundle` accepts `all` and stages converted-trained f32/q8/q4 entries into one q4-defaulted selector root with real file-backed selector/model/manifest smokes for all three entries.
current_boundary_safetensors_inspection_delta: `tinyrustlm-slm-pack inspect-safetensors` reads safetensors headers, validates dtype sizes, tensor shapes, byte offsets, and contiguous coverage, then writes checksum-bearing line reports before future raw-source conversion.
current_boundary_safetensors_source_plan_delta: `tinyrustlm-slm-pack plan-safetensors-source` maps inspected safetensors tensor directories to supported raw f32 trained-source shapes, checks required names and exact dimensions, records copy/decode actions and raw output files, and emits a mapping checksum before extraction.
current_boundary_safetensors_source_extraction_delta: `tinyrustlm-slm-pack extract-safetensors-source` reuses checked safetensors source plans, optionally enforces the candidate-review route, advertises that tail in primary CLI usage, copies F32 payloads, decodes F16/BF16 payloads to raw f32, writes reviewed trained-source manifests with `source_review_*` rows when review-bound, and hands output to `validate-source`.
current_boundary_safetensors_trained_conversion_delta: `tinyrustlm-slm-pack convert-safetensors-trained` accepts local TinyRustLM tensor names or Hugging Face Llama aliases, validates output quantization before extraction, optionally binds it to the candidate review, advertises that tail in primary CLI usage, preserves the raw f32 source directory plus review checksum, validates it, and writes converted-trained f32/q8_0/q4_0 `.slm` artifacts plus manifests.
current_boundary_safetensors_browser_bundle_delta: `tinyrustlm-slm-pack browser-safetensors-trained-bundle` accepts safetensors input, source shape, preserved source directory, output browser root, f32/q8_0/q4_0/all selector, optional eval cases, and optional candidate review with tested primary CLI usage text, then enforces reviewed q8-first browser-preferred quantization or `all`, resolves local review `eval_cases_route` when the review is supplied without explicit eval cases, rejects explicit eval drift before extraction, appends the reviewed eval route into generated sidecars, revalidates local reference-prompt/eval-case artifact rows when file-backed, and stages selector evidence with copied source manifests, copied source-review sidecars carrying tokenizer-import rows, browser-routed source-validation sidecars, and browser-routed runtime-smoke sidecars; the local BPE fixture now has one all-quant test proving selector validation plus copied review/validation/runtime/eval evidence and browser-visible Tokenizer Import plus Source Validation evidence for f32/q8_0/q4_0.
current_boundary_safetensors_candidate_review_delta: `tinyrustlm-slm-pack review-safetensors-candidate` writes a no-crate pre-extraction real-checkpoint report binding safetensors plan evidence to source id plus SHA-shaped source revision, hex64 config/tokenizer/reference-output checksums, config/tokenizer/license/reference/eval routes, local config/tokenizer JSON artifact status/kind/checksum/byte/detail evidence including tokenizer version/added-token/pipeline summaries when routes resolve to files, local license/reference-prompt/eval-case artifact status/kind/checksum/byte/detail evidence when routes resolve to files, source config/tokenizer route tails advertised by primary CLI usage, required compatible local BPE tokenizer JSON import into manifest-ready tokenizer import status/count/checksum rows, route-only and non-byte-fallback BPE rejection, exact byte estimates including imported BPE tokenizer section bytes, selector-budget evidence, `browser_admission_preference_order=q8_0,q4_0,f32`, q8-first browser admission preference, browser eval-route binding through generated eval sidecar echoes, context/KV budgets, downstream extraction/conversion/browser enforcement with tokenizer-import checksum drift rejection, reviewed local BPE all-quant fixture staging that now fails closed before selector admission unless honest assistant-quality evidence passes, and checksum carry-forward into source_review evidence.
current_boundary_smollm2_gqa_gbpe_delta: Runtime generation, model validation, native `.slm` admission, source tensor planning, safetensors planning, and tokenizer serialization now support grouped-query attention plus GPT2/ByteLevel BPE as `gpt2-bpe-v1` / `GBPE`; `smollm2-135m-instruct-bpe` planning binds vocab 49152, hidden 576, 30 layers, 9 query heads, 3 KV heads, tied output, context 8192, 272 tensors, and K/V projection rows of 192 while preserving chat special markers atomically. This is an instruction-capable compatibility lane only; product quality still requires a converted SmolLM2 `.slm` to pass honest eval through the same UI/runtime path.
current_boundary_browser_converted_trained_source_evidence_delta: Converted-trained browser bundle entries preserve reviewed source identity by copying `source.manifest` to `evidence/<candidate-id>/converted-trained.source.manifest`, copying candidate-review reports to `evidence/<candidate-id>/converted-trained.source.review` when present, writing `evidence/<candidate-id>/converted-trained.source.validation`, carrying selector source-review and source-validation routes, and browser-verifying source manifest plus review and validation sidecar fields including source model id, SHA, tokenizer import rows, source manifest checksum, tensor count, tied-output flag, and next conversion gate before selected model bytes while rejecting selector review omission, malformed sidecar field drift, tokenizer-import drift, source-validation drift, or source-review/eval route mismatch.
current_boundary_browser_converted_trained_admission_delta: Converted-trained selector entries now carry `admission_path=../evidence/<candidate-id>/converted-trained.admission` plus checksum; the admission sidecar echoes source/review/validation/runtime/eval routes, candidate bytes/checksums, tokenizer checksum, promotion decision, selector status, public claim status, and required next gate, and the browser verifies it after eval evidence and before model bytes while `converted-trained-admission-drift` proves semantic admission drift stops loading.
current_boundary_browser_converted_trained_source_identity_delta: Converted-trained selector entries preserve reviewed source kind, source id, and source model shape from copied source snapshots; app.js verifies fetched source identity before converted model bytes, safetensors bundle tests bind `trained-export` checkpoint identity, heritable artifact ids include source identity, and `converted-trained-source-identity-drift` proves checksum-matched source-id drift stops before q8 bytes.
